namespace middleware.ratelimit;

import redis;

--- 60 requests per rolling 60s window, keyed on the client address.
---
--- `redis.rate_limit` is INCR + EXPIRE in one Lua script. The hand-rolled
--- read-modify-write this replaced got two things wrong: concurrent
--- requests could both read the same count and both write count+1, and the
--- window was per-process, so N replicas meant an effective limit of 60xN.
---
--- `request.client_ip()` reads `X-Forwarded-For` only through the
--- `trusted_proxies` list in `app.jwc`; with none configured it is the
--- socket peer. That is the whole rule (config.md §3.3) and it is why this
--- no longer hand-reads `cf-connecting-ip`.
middleware RateLimit {
    let ip = request.client_ip();
    let allowed = redis.rate_limit("rl:" + string.of($ip), 60, 60);

    if (!$allowed) {
        throw TooManyRequests("juda ko'p so'rov");
    }
}
